Floors and steps for partial preemption of elastic RayClusters.

Partial preemption needs to know how far a victim may shrink. Workload
minCount keeps its upstream meaning, so the floor travels in two Workload
annotations instead: kueue.x-k8s.io/reclaim-min-counts and
kueue.x-k8s.io/podset-count-steps. With the PartialPreemption gate on, the job
reconciler writes them when it builds the Workload of an elastic RayCluster:
floor = minReplicas and step 1 for each single-host worker group.
EnsureWorkloadSlices keeps them current on the slice it returns, in a
metadata-only update that leaves spec, minCount and admission alone. Multi-host
groups, the head, non-elastic RayClusters, RayJobs and RayServices get no entry.
With the gate off, nothing is written or updated.

